A||||18||86GT-FstBk||Exhaust Comparison||||5||
Z||000000||86GT-FstBk||09-04-2000||02:14 PM||||I'm just wanting to know if anyone has ever bought the stock exaust system from the Fiero Store and if anyone ever bought the Ocelot exaust system.  If so how is the performance of each?<P>Thanks,<BR>Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||09-04-2000||05:02 PM||||I don't have either systems but through talking with other fiero owners and research on this subject I have learned this. The stock exhaust system and the Ocelot exhaust system are about same quality; crap. Those exhaust systems don't have mandrel bent tubing and are made of aluminized steel, not stainless steel. Your factory exhaust system is made of 409 stainless steel which will surface rust but won't rust through like mild steel will. I have read threads on this forum about the Ocelot exhaust system creating a high-pitched resonance sound that does not sound very good.<P>If you want a quality exhaust system that will sound like your factory system with a little louder and deeper rumble than get the Borla exhaust system. The Borla exhaust system is made of 304 stainless steel mandrel bent tubing that won't rust at all. According to Fiero Parts and Appraisals it is dynoed at a 7 HP gain over the stock system. I got mine from Dason Auto in California 310-6777185. You can also get it from Fiero Parts and Appraisals. <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com</A>  I chose to get mine from Dason auto because Fiero parts and Appraisals won't sell the system with the tips and I wanted the system with the tips.<P>It all boils down to the old saying that you get what you pay for. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/003_0a_5.jpg">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 09-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||09-04-2000||11:52 PM||||after ditching the Ocelot unit that came on my car from the previous owner we saw a 4hp and 10lbft gain at the wheels... (changed to 2.5" single in single out 2 chamber 40 series flowmaster) might want to check out  <A HREF="http://www.goravin.com" TARGET=_blank>www.goravin.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||09-05-2000||09:51 AM||||Hey 88Formula, how much did the Borla Exhaust system cost you from Dason auto?||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||09-05-2000||05:34 PM||||$550 but that was with the dual chrome tips. If you bought the system without those tips and then bought those tips separately from Borla and had them welded it would cost you more.||||reg||1
