Z||000013||BBBAD GT||09-06-2000||10:05 PM||||Actually, its a totally custom exhaust for the 350.  Like I stated, its running a big ol flowmaster muffler, with custom bent pipes.  Those painted 'shields' above the pipes are nothing more than just the stock square panel every GT rear valance has, Chris just painted it gray, like other items under the decklid/hood.  Check out the pics to see.  He really did a good job mixing it all up, espically the black roof job 'al la late model camaro'.  I love it.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000014||fierosound||09-08-2000||12:49 AM||||Just a couple pics of the system going on my car.  Just got the BORLA system with tips from Fiero Parts <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroparts.com</A>   and my FOCOA headers from Fiero Conversions (in Canada).  Just waiting for custom pushrods to reinstall top end of engine, prior to installing new engine in car.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/headers.jpg">    <P>Engine details in another forum   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005508.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005508.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||rockcrawl||09-08-2000||01:28 PM||||I had the Oscelot system with Ansa resonting tips on one of my cars, the previous owner installed it. I took it off in favor of a F-body flowmaster when I installed the 3.8. I did't have any complaints about it. Sounded about the same as stock, maybe a little louder. The 3.8/Flowmaster sounds awesome, but not too loud. Aluminized pipe will last as long as I need it to, and stainless is just too expensive IMO.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
